{"abstract":"A bicycle node network is a wayfinding system targeted at recreational cyclists, consisting of numbered signposts placed alongside already existing infrastructure. Bicycle node networks are becoming increasingly popular as they encourage sustainable tourism and rural cycling, while also being flexible and cost-effective to implement. However, the lack of a formalized methodology and data-driven tools for the planning of such networks is a hindrance to their adaptation on a larger scale. To address this need, we present the BikeNodePlanner: A fully open-source decision support tool, consisting of modular Python scripts to be run in the free and open-source geographic information system QGIS. The BikeNodePlanner allows the user to evaluate and compare bicycle node network plans through a wide range of metrics, such as land use, proximity to points of interest, and elevation across the network. The BikeNodePlanner provides data-driven decision support for bicycle node network planning and can hence be of great use for regional planning, cycling tourism, and the promotion of rural cycling.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vybornova, Anastassia","Vierø, Ane Rahbek","Krogh Hansen, Kirsten","Szell, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830686"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Complexity Science Hub"],"keyword":["Bicycle node networks","Cycling tourism","Rural cycling"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Coastal and Rural Tourism"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bikenodeplanner a data driven decision support tool for bicycle node network planning","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-830686","identifier":[{"id":"105013514535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-b79f528e-08f7-4951-a789-c8ca67494c80"],"keyword":["Bicycle node networks","Cycling tourism","Rural cycling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-75C8C2884B07FA28CDAC47203A615527"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Mobility, Space, Place and Urban Studies (MOSPUS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Coastal and Rural Tourism"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"at","key":"complexity science hub","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Complexity Science Hub","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anastassia","key":"vybornovapau","last":"Vybornova","name":"Vybornova, Anastassia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","country":"dk","first":"Ane Rahbek","key":"vierøpau","last":"Vierø","locid":"68c94971-c40a-4223-af24-f2b476d7f7ba","name":"Vierø, Ane Rahbek","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Kirsten","key":"kroghhansenpau","last":"Krogh Hansen","name":"Krogh Hansen, Kirsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","first":"Michael","key":"szellpau","last":"Szell","name":"Szell, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/23998083251355999","issn":["23998083","23998091"],"issn_org":["23998083"],"issue":"7","journal":"Environment and Planning B: Urban Analytics and City Science","pages":"1771-1780","paperid":"23998083251355999","status":"p","title":"Environment and Planning B: Urban Analytics and City Science","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013514535"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-b79f528e-08f7-4951-a789-c8ca67494c80"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"BikeNodePlanner : A data-driven decision support tool for bicycle node network planning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830686","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Walking is the most sustainable form of urban mobility, but is compromised by uncomfortable or unhealthy sun exposure, which is an increasing problem due to global warming. Shade from buildings can provide cooling and protection for pedestrians, but the extent of this potential benefit is unknown. Here we explore the potential for shaded walking, using building footprints and street networks from both synthetic and real cities. We introduce a route choice model with a sun avoidance parameter α and define the CoolWalkability metric to measure opportunities for walking in shade. We derive analytically that on a regular grid with constant building heights, CoolWalkability is independent of α, and that the grid provides no CoolWalkability benefit for shade-seeking individuals compared to the shortest path. However, variations in street geometry and building heights create such benefits. We further uncover that the potential for shaded routing differs between grid-like and irregular street networks, forms local clusters, and is sensitive to the mapped network geometry. Our research identifies the limitations and potential of shade for cool, active travel, and is a first step towards a rigorous understanding of shade provision for sustainable mobility in cities.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Wolf, Henrik","Vierø, Ane Rahbek","Szell, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818236"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","TU Dresden"],"keyword":["Route choice model","Sun exposure","Urban mobility"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coolwalks for active mobility in urban street networks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-025-97200-2","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["M.Sz. acknowledges funding from EU Horizon Project JUST STREETS (Grant agreement ID: 101104240)"],"id":"S01-000.00-818236","identifier":[{"id":"105003781891","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-42619e77-eb69-452d-aae1-f852b44d6085"],"keyword":["CoolWalkability metric","route choice model","shaded walking","sun exposure","urban mobility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C2DE2380C70C2E1CF9BA661C62CFD469"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-025-97200-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-97200-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"tu dresden","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TU Dresden","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"wolfpau","last":"Wolf","name":"Wolf, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ane Rahbek","key":"vierøpau","last":"Vierø","locid":"45b600aa-d6c7-4c4b-91b3-1d934aec4402","name":"Vierø, Ane Rahbek","orcid":"0000-0002-2404-7271","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"szellpau","last":"Szell","locid":"2ef641d0-bd79-425b-8b12-b58d74b993ae","name":"Szell, Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-3022-2483","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-025-97200-2","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"14911","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003781891"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-42619e77-eb69-452d-aae1-f852b44d6085"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CoolWalks for active mobility in urban street networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818236","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Spatial data science is an emerging field building on geographic information science, geography, and data science. Here we first discuss the definition and history of the field, arguing that it indeed warrants a new label. Then, we present the design of our course Geospatial Data Science at IT University of Copenhagen and discuss the importance of teaching not just spatial data science tools but also spatial and critical thinking. We conclude with a perspective on the potential future for spatial data science, arguing that qualitative theory and methods will continue to play an important role despite new GeoAI-related advances. ‘Spatial data science’ er et spirende felt, der udspringer af både geografisk informationsvidenskab, geografi og data science. I denne artikel diskuterer vi først begrebet spatial data science, introducerer dets historie og argumenterer for, at det repræsenterer et nybrud i forhold til tidligere tendenser indenfor GIS og geodata. Herefter præsenterer vi vores overvejelser om undervisning i spatial data science i forbindelse med udviklingen af kurset Geospatial Data Science på IT Universitet i København. Vi understreger vigtigheden i ikke bare at undervise i praktiske anvendelser af geodata, men også at lære de studerende geografisk og kritisk tænkning. Afslutningsvis diskuterer vi fremtiden for spatial data science, og argumenterer for, at geografisk teori og metoder vil forblive relevante trods af den stigende indflydelse fra GeoAI.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Vierø, Ane Rahbek","Szell, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789551"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data science","GeoAI","Python","Spatial data science","Teaching"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"teaching spatial data science","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.54337/ojs.perspektiv.v23i44.8383","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789551","ids":["itu-53ec5342-d7d8-40d7-a12f-ffea725c870d"],"keyword":["Data science","GeoAI","Python","Teaching","spatial data science"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-73C28C02F16D3E44D81CA6038A6757CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.54337/ojs.perspektiv.v23i44.8383","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ane Rahbek","key":"vierøpau","last":"Vierø","locid":"45b600aa-d6c7-4c4b-91b3-1d934aec4402","name":"Vierø, Ane Rahbek","orcid":"0000-0002-2404-7271","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"szellpau","last":"Szell","locid":"2ef641d0-bd79-425b-8b12-b58d74b993ae","name":"Szell, Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-3022-2483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-53ec5342-d7d8-40d7-a12f-ffea725c870d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Teaching spatial data science","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789551","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Cycling is a key ingredient for a sustainability shift of Denmark's transportation system. To increase cycling rates, better bicycle infrastructure networks are required. Planning such networks requires high-quality infrastructure data, yet the quality of bicycle infrastructure data is understudied. Here, we compare the two largest open data sets on dedicated bicycle infrastructure in Denmark, OpenStreetMap (OSM) and GeoDanmark, in a countrywide data quality assessment, asking whether the data are good enough for network-based analysis of cycling conditions. We find that neither of the data sets is of sufficient quality, and that data conflation is necessary to obtain a more complete data set. Our analysis of the spatial variation of data quality suggests that rural areas are more prone to incomplete data. We demonstrate that the prevalent method of using infrastructure density as a proxy for data completeness is not suitable for bicycle infrastructure data, and that matching of corresponding features is thus necessary to assess data completeness. Based on our data quality assessment, we recommend strategic mapping efforts toward data completeness, consistent standards to support comparability between different data sources, and increased focus on data topology to ensure high-quality bicycle network data.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vierø, Ane Rahbek","Vybornova, Anastassia","Szell, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730156"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bicycle infrastructure","Bicycle networks","Open data","OpenStreetMap","Spatial data quality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how good is open bicycle network data a countrywide case study of denmark","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://michael.szell.net/downloads/viero2024hgo.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Danish Ministry of Transport. Grant Number: CP21-033"],"id":"S01-000.00-730156","identifier":[{"id":"85189989316","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-00865963-6ad8-41ef-a860-5258d1c67b74"],"keyword":["Bicycle infrastructure","Bicycle networks","Open data","OpenStreetMap","Spatial data quality"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-911D040BFB319479D9E23F2E9AD6FDA1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://michael.szell.net/downloads/viero2024hgo.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ane Rahbek","key":"vierøpau","last":"Vierø","locid":"45b600aa-d6c7-4c4b-91b3-1d934aec4402","name":"Vierø, Ane Rahbek","orcid":"0000-0002-2404-7271","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anastassia","key":"vybornovapau","last":"Vybornova","locid":"60b2482e-a0d3-4094-8723-76ea44a33c30","name":"Vybornova, Anastassia","orcid":"0000-0001-6915-2561","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"szellpau","last":"Szell","locid":"2ef641d0-bd79-425b-8b12-b58d74b993ae","name":"Szell, Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-3022-2483","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/gean.12400","issn":["15384632"],"journal":"Geographical Analysis","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Geographical Analysis"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189989316"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-00865963-6ad8-41ef-a860-5258d1c67b74"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How Good Is Open Bicycle Network Data? A Countrywide Case Study of Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730156","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"High-quality data on existing bicycle infrastructure are a requirement for evidence-based bicycle network planning, which supports a green transition of human mobility. However, this requirement is rarely met: Data from governmental agencies or crowdsourced projects like OpenStreetMap often suffer from unknown, heterogeneous, or low quality. Currently available tools for road network data quality assessment often fail to account for network topology, spatial heterogeneity, and bicycle-specific data characteristics. To fill these gaps, we introduce BikeDNA, an open-source tool for reproducible quality assessment tailored to bicycle infrastructure data with a focus on network structure and connectivity. BikeDNA performs either a standalone analysis of one data set or a comparative analysis between OpenStreetMap and a reference data set, including feature matching. Data quality metrics are considered both globally for the entire study area and locally on grid cell level, thus exposing spatial variation in data quality. Interactive maps and HTML/PDF reports are generated to facilitate the visual exploration and communication of results. BikeDNA supports quality assessments of bicycle infrastructure data for a wide range of applications -- from urban planning to OpenStreetMap data improvement or network research for sustainable mobility.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vierø, Ane Rahbek","Vybornova, Anastassia","Szell, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695240"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bicycle networks","Open source software","OpenStreetMap","Spatial data quality","Volunteered Geographic Information"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bikedna a tool for bicycle infrastructure data and network assessment","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.01223","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695240","identifier":[{"id":"85162649377","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-44371a4f-0e57-4472-a28d-c4e445a6c87b"],"keyword":["OpenStreetMap","bicycle networks","open-source software","spatial data quality","volunteered geographic information"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5F5FCA5C4375303628AC6A4E23BEEE6D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.01223","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ane Rahbek","key":"vierøpau","last":"Vierø","locid":"45b600aa-d6c7-4c4b-91b3-1d934aec4402","name":"Vierø, Ane Rahbek","orcid":"0000-0002-2404-7271","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anastassia","key":"vybornovapau","last":"Vybornova","locid":"60b2482e-a0d3-4094-8723-76ea44a33c30","name":"Vybornova, Anastassia","orcid":"0000-0001-6915-2561","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"szellpau","last":"Szell","locid":"2ef641d0-bd79-425b-8b12-b58d74b993ae","name":"Szell, Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-3022-2483","rank":3,"rol